3194139534696 true] [17592186179699 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303904 13194139534696 true] [17592186179699 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303911 13194139534696 true] [17592186179699 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303918 13194139534696 true] [17592186179699 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303925 13194139534696 true] [17592186179703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303960 13194139534696 true] [17592186179703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303967 13194139534696 true] [17592186179703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303974 13194139534696 true] [17592186179703 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303981 13194139534696 true] [17592186179920 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534696 true] [17592186179920 1100 "Consider the transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=3u+v-2,\\,y=u-2v+1.\n$$\n\nLet $P(3,2)$ be a point in the $uv$-plane. Suppose that the image of $P$ under the action of $T$ is the point ${P}^{′}$ in the $xy$-plane. What are the coordinates of ${P}^{′}?$" 13194139534696 true] [17592186179920 1100 "Consider the transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$x = 3u + v - 2, y = u - 2v + 1$.\nLet $P(3, 2)$ be a point in the $uv$-plane. Suppose that the image of $P$ under the action of $T$ is the point $P^{′}$ in the $xy$-plane. What are the coordinates of $P^{′}$?" 13194139534696 false] [17592186179920 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3u+v-2 \\\\ u-2v+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u+v \\\\ u-2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the image of $P$ under the action of $T,$ we first create a column vector $u$ containing the coordinates of $P:$\n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nApplying $T$ to $u,$ we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of ${P}^{′}$ are $(9,0).$" 13194139534696 true] [17592186179921 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534696 true] [17592186179921 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/a4a1d43bc68a44db24d22767630573ebd9aafb646196e212640c24f2650e7b17.png)\n\nConsider the triangle $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1-u}.\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the image of $Δ$ in the $xy$-plane under the action of $T?$" 13194139534696 true] [17592186179921 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3706/Source/Images/q-124103.png)\n\nConsider the triangle $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n$Δ = {(u, v): 0 \\le u \\le 1, 0 \\le v \\le 1 - u}$.\nThe transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nWhich of the following gives the image of $Δ$ in the $xy$-plane under the action of $T$?" 13194139534696 false] [17592186179921 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation is already in matrix form \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the boundary of $Δ$ to the boundary of the image. So, to find the image of $Δ,$ we find the images of each side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/0d736c2e3fa2c4ba1872b045b8bdcf4def98a24337683e368bec337b810b6acb.png)\n\n          \n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing all vertices of our triangle:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertices of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(0,-1),(1,0),$ and $(-2,0).$\n\nDrawing this region in the $xy$-plane, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/1aed421f9d6458fb8b72a44c83703b3f1c0475cee9ef9ec2f0a4cfcaad74d7fc.png)\n\n          \n\nFinally, since $det(A)=3>0,$ this transformation preserves orientation." 13194139534696 true] [17592186180017 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534696 true] [17592186180017 1100 "Consider the affine transformation $T$, defined as\n\n$x = v - u, y = u + v - 1$.\n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" 13194139534696 false] [17592186180017 1100 "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=v-u,\\,y=u+v-1.\n$$\n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" 13194139534696 true] [17592186180017 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}v-u \\\\ u+v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+v \\\\ u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 1=-2.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|-2|=2.\n$$" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303869 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303870 13194139534696 true] [17592186303869 1089 "q-124144" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303869 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534696 true] [17592186303869 1100 "Consider the transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=-v+u+2,\\,y=u+v-1.\n$$\n\nLet $P(4,1)$ be a point in the $uv$-plane. Suppose that the image of $P$ under the action of $T$ is the point ${P}^{′}$ in the $xy$-plane. What are the coordinates of ${P}^{′}?$" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303869 1113 #uuid "c30de37e-94eb-5824-8c19-5f0e87550d0b" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303869 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-v+u+2 \\\\ u+v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the image of $P$ under the action of $T,$ we first create a column vector $u$ containing the coordinates of $P:$\n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nApplying $T$ to $u,$ we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of ${P}^{′}$ are $(5,4).$" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303871 13194139534696 true] [17592186303870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303872 13194139534696 true] [17592186303870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303873 13194139534696 true] [17592186303870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303874 13194139534696 true] [17592186303870 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303875 13194139534696 true] [17592186303870 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534696 true] [17592186303870 1041 "selection" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303870 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303873 13194139534696 true] [17592186303870 1110 #uuid "3c3c23de-5cfc-57e5-a014-ffb79ba7607c" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303871 1034 "(4,4)" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303871 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534696 true] [17592186303871 1111 #uuid "1693998f-ab45-5bec-a343-cc5d77a5ad9b" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303872 1034 "(2,5)" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303872 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534696 true] [17592186303872 1111 #uuid "510b68a7-d999-56c8-8bf9-ccdea66bbc9b" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303873 1034 "(5,4)" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303873 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534696 true] [17592186303873 1111 #uuid "a09dca29-a5e4-5ae7-803d-4417beab6aa8" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303874 1034 "(5,-5)" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303874 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534696 true] [17592186303874 1111 #uuid "84354f8c-7b1e-581b-9d72-d44901b4a6ab" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303875 1034 "(4,-5)" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303875 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534696 true] [17592186303875 1111 #uuid "97b03400-a304-590f-8bf4-358a28ece2f7" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303876 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303877 13194139534696 true] [17592186303876 1089 "q-124151" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303876 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534696 true] [17592186303876 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/33f7326ffe8318fca915e8cc7e02a2a4c280dd9377066f1870f3bb8067b22eb0.png)\n\nConsider the segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ above, and the transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2u+3v+2,\\,y=v-2u.\n$$\n\nThe image of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ under the action of $T$ is the segment $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}$ in the $xy$-plane. Which of the following diagrams shows $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}?$" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303876 1113 #uuid "3187ec42-ba90-5620-adf4-a7bfe030aeac" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303876 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u+3v+2 \\\\ v-2u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,2u+3v \\\\ -2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ to the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}.$ So, to find the image of $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ we find the images of each endpoint.\n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing the endpoints of our segment:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the endpoints of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(-5,3)$ and $(10,0).$\n\nDrawing this segment in the $xy$-plane, we get the following: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/e4bea3edd3fcde575e68e36e08fc4186863b12450802eb0ee37c841975983486.png)" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303878 13194139534696 true] [17592186303877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303879 13194139534696 true] [17592186303877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303880 13194139534696 true] [17592186303877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303881 13194139534696 true] [17592186303877 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303882 13194139534696 true] [17592186303877 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 131