nThe image of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ under the action of $T$ is the segment $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}$ in the $xy$-plane. Which of the following diagrams shows $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}?$" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303890 1113 #uuid "e5578bdc-3ff0-534a-8da8-40c48db3f6bd" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303890 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u+2v-2 \\\\ v-u+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2u+2v \\\\ -u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ to the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}}.$ So, to find the image of $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ we find the images of each endpoint.\n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing the endpoints of our segment:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the endpoints of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(-6,2)$ and $(8,1).$\n\nDrawing this segment in the $xy$-plane, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/8e57b4d47ef3c6ad1b1d70a97126aa865c4481ee67e16eaf4e79c09e3146b30d.png)" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303892 13194139534696 true] [17592186303891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303893 13194139534696 true] [17592186303891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303894 13194139534696 true] [17592186303891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303895 13194139534696 true] [17592186303891 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303896 13194139534696 true] [17592186303891 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534696 true] [17592186303891 1041 "selection" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303891 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303896 13194139534696 true] [17592186303891 1110 #uuid "63a8b844-021e-5a76-8e45-520da6a5cb61" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303892 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/299dcfa34c32c5e51c78b585514308806dab67fd3c9f5d3d80e492b3e424960d.png" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303892 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534696 true] [17592186303892 1111 #uuid "d5815bdb-f2b2-51d5-9f30-3692a37dac43" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303893 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/947907e5a3581626420616f119cc126c08718a7d4c9323032fa3e1774dcc9537.png" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303893 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534696 true] [17592186303893 1111 #uuid "c9387147-3c52-590d-ae19-083d431ffa62" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303894 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/449acd0aaaf07a8116faf0fee0936751bd375dd7eb270fd7c4adee3e381c8641.png" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303894 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534696 true] [17592186303894 1111 #uuid "6a126133-5eef-5ba0-abf8-e33e480f302d" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303895 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/43f482344220e14c9633691ca880da0b310ece86779841ad4bac909c230dafa3.png" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303895 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534696 true] [17592186303895 1111 #uuid "574b78e8-724a-56a3-b25b-cc2cd5cc85cc" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303896 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/8e57b4d47ef3c6ad1b1d70a97126aa865c4481ee67e16eaf4e79c09e3146b30d.png" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303896 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534696 true] [17592186303896 1111 #uuid "76ea7656-b3a5-5f8b-8d72-4c7bb94d4b23" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303897 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303898 13194139534696 true] [17592186303897 1089 "q-124192" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303897 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534696 true] [17592186303897 1100 "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2v+u+1,\\,y=u-v-2.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=-3$\n- The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303897 1113 #uuid "06e1c006-ef77-5600-9c9c-1814cfed601d" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303897 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2v+u+1 \\\\ u-v-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+2v \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot 1=-3.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303898 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303899 13194139534696 true] [17592186303898 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303900 13194139534696 true] [17592186303898 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303901 13194139534696 true] [17592186303898 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303902 13194139534696 true] [17592186303898 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303903 13194139534696 true] [17592186303898 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534696 true] [17592186303898 1041 "selection" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303898 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303903 13194139534696 true] [17592186303898 1110 #uuid "774cccfc-2e55-57ca-abe5-29c616377f1d" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303899 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303899 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534696 true] [17592186303899 1111 #uuid "d3be1eae-2cd4-56b5-801c-f6fe5e399b6c" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303900 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303900 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534696 true] [17592186303900 1111 #uuid "71ec5ded-460c-5c66-8ed0-87fcd3c087e5" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303901 1034 "I only" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303901 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534696 true] [17592186303901 1111 #uuid "63c535af-7cd8-5614-a0e9-9b6fbd753626" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303902 1034 "III only" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303902 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534696 true] [17592186303902 1111 #uuid "5a1be5d3-bc33-5f8c-913f-2c87703fa2c3" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303903 1034 "II only" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303903 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534696 true] [17592186303903 1111 #uuid "5fac8f54-711e-5e1c-ac70-e382b4642d76" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303904 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303905 13194139534696 true] [17592186303904 1089 "q-124322" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303904 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534696 true] [17592186303904 1100 "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=u+3v-5,\\,y=2v+u-4.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=1$\n- The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303904 1113 #uuid "e5f774fd-e4fc-5b69-88ef-de7d2e0c0984" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303904 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+3v-5 \\\\ 2v+u-4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+3v \\\\ u+2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is false. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 3=-1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303906 13194139534696 true] [17592186303905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303907 13194139534696 true] [17592186303905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303908 13194139534696 true] [17592186303905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303909 13194139534696 true] [17592186303905 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303910 13194139534696 true] [17592186303905 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534696 true] [17592186303905 1041 "selection" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303905 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303907 13194139534696 true] [17592186303905 1110 #uuid "f2426634-cac1-5dbc-9533-c56bee455598" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303906 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303906 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534696 true] [17592186303906 1111 #uuid "c5080850-0f92-5e66-bf9e-eba895f1b27f" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303907 1034 "I only" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303907 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534696 true] [17592186303907 1111 #uuid "b02df7f6-72aa-5b29-a8c7-e7f68876b230" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303908 1034 "III only" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303908 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534696 true] [17592186303908 1111 #uuid "133afa23-fbbc-530a-85ee-d10e18393d9a" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303909 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303909 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534696 true] [17592186303909 1111 #uuid "265654b9-33a4-59a1-bc49-6f43a3af9c80" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303910 1034 "II only" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303910 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534696 true] [17592186303910 1111 #uuid "e5359659-7028-57fd-948a-564059763874" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303911 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303912 13194139534696 true] [17592186303911 1089 "q-124326" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303911 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534696 true] [17592186303911 1100 "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=u-1,\\,y=u-v-2.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]$\n- $det(A)=-1$\n- The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303911 1113 #uuid "f53de4b4-b46c-561f-a45d-98fcac1e0352" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303911 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-1 \\\\ u-v-2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 0=-1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303913 13194139534696 true] [17592186303912 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303914 13194139534696 true] [1759