t the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2v+1 \\\\ 4u-v-5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2v \\\\ 4u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is false. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=0\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot (-2)=8.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $det(A)>0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303927 13194139534696 true] [17592186303926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303928 13194139534696 true] [17592186303926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303929 13194139534696 true] [17592186303926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303930 13194139534696 true] [17592186303926 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303931 13194139534696 true] [17592186303926 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534696 true] [17592186303926 1041 "selection" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303926 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303930 13194139534696 true] [17592186303926 1110 #uuid "a799794b-0005-5d4d-bc0e-e6ffba540047" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303927 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303927 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534696 true] [17592186303927 1111 #uuid "6b6f32d9-7dc2-5632-8c33-2ba6c723a826" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303928 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303928 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534696 true] [17592186303928 1111 #uuid "34b3eae8-e1ba-5d0f-8953-964f56790324" 13194139534696 true] [175921863