reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/6be30b91e0526e28530b4c5cfff6c0c5e7be53a77e587c5eb37a845b6cc0a189.png" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303938 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534696 true] [17592186303938 1111 #uuid "07a9c971-297c-5726-8ca1-44528cca84fa" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303939 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303940 13194139534696 true] [17592186303939 1089 "q-124569" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303939 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534696 true] [17592186303939 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/deff964a1833339681fc38b30e32ebd3081e7ba1c4b5aabd0f4998f60a2aa78c.png)\n\nConsider the triangle $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le v\\le 1,\\,\\frac{v-1}{2}\\le u\\le \\frac{1-v}{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the image of $Δ$ in the $xy$-plane under the action of $T?$" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303939 1113 #uuid "e48d3f9e-79f6-5f88-9764-fe40dc9cde3f" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303939 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation is already in matrix form \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the boundary of $Δ$ to the boundary of the image. So, to find the image of $Δ,$ we find the images of each side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/daefc9e14775a955e5210f965e474c06bc7cac1df9306941b73190cc8bf62219.png)\n\n          \n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing all vertices of our triangle:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertices of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(-3,-2),(-1,2),$ and $(0,2).$ \n\nDrawing this region in the $xy$-plane, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/94a2a90dae43d1edb1f0154a8c7ac60b8c35352fd72d5193014b9bba204d192f.png)\n\n          \n\nFinally, since $det(A)=-1<0,$ this transformation is not orientation-preserving." 13194139534696 true] [17592186303940 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303941 13194139534696 true] [17592186303940 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303942 13194139534696 true] [17592186303940 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303943 13194139534696 true] [17592186303940 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303944 13194139534696 true] [17592186303940 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303945 13194139534696 true] [17592186303940 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534696 true] [17592186303940 1041 "selection" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303940 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303943 13194139534696 true] [17592186303940 1110 #uuid "26ac11aa-8ae5-5483-8191-35b466449001" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303941 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/9ebbc28d7bf9b1ec3e5adb15a036570f1a7025d0dcedab7f61610c09b0c4c423.png" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303941 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534696 true] [17592186303941 1111 #uuid "803efcb7-e723-5486-8fb5-1981680106bf" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303942 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/f17eeed2b5ab0b065ab0c4c7c7c669108ce4f0d8de8f69979316d12c2885d73e.png" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303942 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534696 true] [17592186303942 1111 #uuid "10a35c72-c612-5acd-b619-867039402deb" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303943 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/e181f53d2f99a2374739769ea5e5837de0acf8526717f0607e0e81dba4da0c1e.png" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303943 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534696 true] [17592186303943 1111 #uuid "f261f6b9-24b2-5b20-b9ad-d372f6348573" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303944 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/01a8419fe9a435734f69c1913764423739b881fd6aa377a08f085e2ea7aab10b.png" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303944 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534696 true] [17592186303944 1111 #uuid "bc29d121-359c-513c-920a-c558b889ac47" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303945 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/a1c56986c6de278a24b0d83d69b26822b4330d815b8f501db7da8f3d10e625da.png" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303945 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534696 true] [17592186303945 1111 #uuid "5d64f1a2-3e15-5e33-9d8e-f0419023a53e" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303946 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303947 13194139534696 true] [17592186303946 1089 "q-124571" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303946 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534696 true] [17592186303946 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/9bfb4e21205db9550d88222e04449b9858137550b957ba652b3e6998dce8025c.png)\n\nConsider the triangle $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le v\\le 1,\\,0\\le u\\le \\frac{1-v}{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the image of $Δ$ in the $xy$-plane under the action of $T?$" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303946 1113 #uuid "c7eb367f-3cc1-5728-9bfc-7b0c473f7380" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303946 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation is already in matrix form \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the boundary of $Δ$ to the boundary of the image. So, to find the image of $Δ,$ we find the images of each side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/194428bede19351ba77866a9ca49f76b38c4327fd0a5e2c219afff9c14b12c28.png)\n\n             \n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing all vertices of our triangle:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertices of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(-2,0),(-1,-1),$ and $(0,2).$\n\nDrawing this region in the $xy$-plane, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/02ab748669496bf50a8809cf822a969d731a18283d52272175fd5b615ef5b765.png)\n\n          \n\nFinally, since $det(A)=2>0,$ this transformation preserves orientation." 13194139534696 true] [17592186303947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303948 13194139534696 true] [17592186303947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303949 13194139534696 true] [17592186303947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303950 13194139534696 true] [17592186303947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303951 13194139534696 true] [17592186303947 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303952 13194139534696 true] [17592186303947 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534696 true] [17592186303947 1041 "selection" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303947 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303948 13194139534696 true] [17592186303947 1110 #uuid "eefff25a-1262-54f4-aba3-375b8c9c00c4" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303948 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/bbddd646e109123853cb4b00898f8042dd9fbb2225e2dd582920035e23e552ac.png" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303948 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534696 true] [17592186303948 1111 #uuid "d6d7ec30-ce77-5207-aaa2-8b5ba75115f5" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303949 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/bd95a6f92fc74e2f3b915de3b6ccda921b1f260ee6080f12a8ca54de243dae1c.png" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303949 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534696 true] [17592186303949 1111 #uuid "c9b2c15b-9e84-5c55-a1f0-7047412da540" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303950 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/e4c3f4e9d984fb71b0f5d34473cca7a825224d4a9db0c4ea18a4e232185b2f48.png" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303950 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534696 true] [17592186303950 1111 #uuid "6e22dc28-3124-56e8-870c-91e5279fd375" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303951 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/3131825a9fd81b0099f9049961c846d2383dcbb3effa5280bdc3818536104746.png" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303951 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534696 true] [17592186303951 1111 #uuid "f3a463f9-7459-5254-8fc7-a77d439630be" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303952 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/60f1c0c294345639995de964b397ee2e31365c35668a24a3a20ad87cdf7d8e6b.png" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303952 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534696 true] [17592186303952 1111 #uuid "a5612992-a821-5d16-b253-f6a811fa8137" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303953 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303954 13194139534696 true] [17592186303953 1089 "q-124650" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303953 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534696 true] [17592186303953 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/d947e13c2b18ce786f03636d174604dd60e715ed0ce1929ff4ac98cf91084a50.png)\n\nConsider the rectangle $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx=3u+2v-2,\\,y=2u+v-1.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the image of $Δ$ in the $xy$-plane under the action of $T?$" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303953 1113 #uuid "0b0635f9-acd6-5529-ae03-8909e67e025f" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303953 1145 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3u+2v-2 \\\\ 2u+v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u+2v \\\\ 2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformation $T$ maps the boundary of $Δ$ to the boundary of the image. So, to find the image of $Δ,$ we find the images of each side.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/d0103ef8cdf76a3f80bd9be6314c2a693cbf9e51fe66f95228ccce1703f6775f.png)\n\n          \n\nTo quickly carry out this calculation, we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing all vertices of our square:\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $b$ in each column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe image of $u$ under $T$ is given by $Au+b.$ So, by applying $T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertices of the image in the $xy$-plane are $(-2,-1),(1,1),(3,2),$ and $(0,0).$\n\nDrawing this region in the $xy$-plane, we get the following: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/0b22301fac2a0d97c0f0d99b3c4d162e8965f5570522754a3e21fa124194f1c0.png)\n\n          \n\nFinally, since $det(A)=-1<0,$ this transformation is not orientation-preserving." 13194139534696 true] [17592186303954 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303955 13194139534696 true] [17592186303954 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303956 13194139534696 true] [17592186303954 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303957 13194139534696 true] [17592186303954 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303958 13194139534696 true] [17592186303954 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303959 13194139534696 true] [17592186303954 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534696 true] [17592186303954 1041 "selection" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303954 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303959 13194139534696 true] [17592186303954 1110 #uuid "e588d2ce-08e1-5b7c-a922-768c9cf803a6" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303955 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039710/assets/509af7e65cf004433f66b89ccf93cce5897956e1b81a90a77a856f7c827450ba.png" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303955 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534696 true] [17592186303955 1111 #uuid "5f845cf8-07d2-5bb1-8e48-6c14a3a965d0" 13194139534696 true] [17592186303956 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Cours